From 7d8ac7297f7591cd90a53ea4f73b1bacc35873c8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ian <ianxu4house@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:43:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ggml-cuda: int8 QK^T in the FA tile kernel for q8_0 K on
 RDNA2 (opt-in GGML_FATTN_KQ8=1, D=256)

The tile flash-attention kernel (fattn-tile.cuh) on gfx1030 is bound by the
half2 QK^T phase: 1.5 B of LDS traffic per MAC, 61% of the kernel at 16K-64K.
With a q8_0 K cache the K values are already 8-bit; this patch keeps them that
way through the dot product:

- K rows are repacked once per launch on the host side into 272-byte rows
  ([256 int8 qs][8 half scales]) by fattn_repack_q8_0_rows (one warp per row,
  16-byte coalesced loads).
- Q is quantised in the kernel prologue to int8 per 32-dim block with its own
  fp32 scale (the KV cache already applies the Hadamard rotation when K is
  quantised, so Q has no outlier dims; per-32 scales are enough).
- QK^T accumulates in int32 with v_dot4 (ggml_cuda_dp4a), one fold to fp32 per
  32-dim block: KQ += d_k * d_q * sumi.  Scales are read from LDS (keeping
  them in VGPRs spilled: 256 VGPR + 31 spills, 1.04-1.11x; from LDS: 221 VGPR,
  no spills, 1.3x).
- The int8 path never goes through launch_fattn's split-KV combine
  (max_blocks_per_sm = 1): the combine path itself loses precision (the
  upstream f16 kernel forced through it goes from max KLD 0.46 to 1.21), and
  the int8 kernel's 30 KB of LDS would otherwise trigger it.

Engaged only when GGML_FATTN_KQ8=1 is set, K is q8_0, D=256 and ncols2=2 (the
Qwen3.8-27B shape); the engine prints a confirm line when it is. Without the
env the kernel is unchanged. Env-gated dump hooks (FATTN_DUMP_DIR,
EVALCB_DUMP_DIR) used for the precision investigation are included; they do
nothing unless set.

Measured on 2x RX 6900 XT (gfx1030), Qwen3.8-27B UD-Q5_K_XL, q8_0 KV:
  test-backend-ops FA (256/256, 6 heads / 1 KV head): 16K 12.81 -> 9.81 ms
  (1.31x), 64K 52.93 -> 40.8 ms (1.30x); 8/8 correctness cases.
  KLD vs bf16 (64x512 mixed zh/en): mean 0.003704 (f16 path 0.003736),
  top-1 agreement 97.29% (97.12%), max 0.558 (0.456).
  End to end (llama-server, -sm tensor, cold-start A/B): prefill 2K/8K flat,
  32K +3.3-3.9%, 128K +11.1% (460.5 -> 511.6 tok/s); decode and VRAM
  unchanged; 32K/128K needles 8/8 + 4/4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
